+# Phase 14 — Multilingual, Currency & India/International Tours
+
+## Implemented
+
+- Reusable English/Marathi translation dictionary and language context.
+- Language selector in the existing header; preference stored in localStorage for guests and `profiles.preferred_language` for authenticated users.
+- Public, reviewed translation lookup for tours, destinations, attractions and itinerary days. Missing/unpublished content falls back to English.
+- Staff translation editor with draft/reviewed/published states.
+- Domestic/international `tours.tour_kind` classification used by the public catalogue filter.
+- INR default and supported currency display selection; language and currency preferences are independent.
+- Configurable exchange-rate provider via server-only environment variables, dated manual-rate fallback, and visible source/status/timestamp.
+- Accepted quotation, booking, payment and refund currency/price snapshots. The display-currency selector does not change a payable quote.
+
+## Rate conventions
+
+Rates are foreign-currency units per INR 1. Example: `INR=1, USD=0.012, EUR=0.011`.
+A rate is indicative only. Accepted quotation totals and their currency are immutable. Do not calculate checkout totals in the browser.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Copy `.env.example` to your local server environment. `CURRENCY_RATE_PROVIDER_URL`, `CURRENCY_RATE_PROVIDER_NAME`, and `CURRENCY_RATE_PROVIDER_API_KEY` are server-only and optional. If no provider or manual rates are configured, only INR is offered; the system does not invent FX rates.
+
+## Migration and verification
+
+```bash
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+npx supabase db push
+pnpm check
+pnpm test
+pnpm build
+```
+
+Manual rates can be configured from `/admin/localization` by an account with `settings.manage`. Translation editing requires `tours.manage`. The rate timestamp and source are stored in the existing `settings` record as `currency_rates_inr_v1`.
+
+Visa, legal, safety and financial-policy translations must be written/reviewed by authorized staff; this feature does not machine-translate or auto-publish them.
